# Issue: joinCtxs grouped the joinable predicates with joinByFst, which
# sorts the groups by key, and the key's Ord (class, then types) is
# string-intern order; the order of the dictionary bindings a definition
# emits followed it, so a one-shot compile and a `bsc -u` batch differed.
# Fix: Util.joinByFstStable keeps the groups in first-occurrence order.
# Pull request: https://github.com/MatX-inc/bsc/pull/186
# Probe: a reduced GrayCounter compiled alone and behind a scrambler that
# interns IsModule before Add must dump the same .bo, hash included.

batching_bo_pair JoinOrder.bsv JoinOrderRoot.bsv JoinOrderScramble.bsv
